Ohio Hanging Rock	Nature Preserve			Active	Arc of Appalachia	Arc of Appalachia	Clean Ohio (acquisition grant)		Remote hill country of the Little Scioto Watershed in northeastern Scioto County. Renowned for immense sandstone outcrops covered with mosses, ferns, and lichens that follow an elevation line just below the ridgetops. Exceptionally rich in fern diversity.	Frederick Rd, Wheelersburg, Ohio 45694; northeastern Scioto County, Little Scioto Watershed	750	Scioto		Bloom	38.815566	-82.786171	86CVR687+6G	Hiking trails;small gravel parking lot;open sunrise to sunset;dogs permitted;trails closed during annual Deer Management Hunt (week after Thanksgiving through Sunday before Christmas);parking not winter-maintained	Baseline seed — previously listed as Tier 8 (private) but Arc of Appalachia is a nonprofit land trust; correctly staged at Tier 7. Future expansion of ~4.76 acres with additional 2.25-mile public trail planned for 2026. Baseline seed confirmed.		https://www.arcofappalachia.org/ohio-hanging-rock;https://www.arcofappalachia.org/visit-ohio-hanging-rock;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/640b875d14fa1852d6031793/t/655905b4c827fe0ff11b0aae/1700332981455/Ohio+Hanging+Rock+Hiking+Guide.pdf		2026-03-31T12:11:18Z	2026-03-31T12:11:18Z
Simon Woods	Nature Preserve			Active	Arc of Appalachia	Arc of Appalachia	Clean Ohio (acquisition grant)		Mature white oak and chestnut oak upland forest, one of the most beautiful in the Arc preserve system. Three headwater streams flowing from ridgetops into Pond Creek. Rocky slopes carpeted with large fern colonies. Key deep-woods warbler breeding species: Kentucky warbler, worm-eating warbler, hooded warbler. Pond Creek exits the farm and winds eastward through Tremper Mound before joining the Scioto River.	8721 Pond Creek-Carey's Run Road, West Portsmouth, Ohio 45663	670	Scioto		Union	38.798858	-83.068080	86CRQWXJ+GQ	Hiking trails;free parking across from homestead at Pond Creek-Carey's Run Rd;historic John Roger Simon Farm homestead with sorghum-making mural (Robert Dafford)	Baseline seed — previously listed as Tier 8 (private) but Arc of Appalachia is a nonprofit land trust; correctly staged at Tier 7. Preserve includes 564-acre John Roger Simon farm (Clean Ohio assisted acquisition) plus 95-acre Noel Hollow expansion. Annual John Roger Simon Sorghum Festival held at preserve. Named trail specifics not confirmed from web search — trail names and lengths PENDING from arcofappalachia.org/visit-simon-woods. Baseline seed confirmed.		https://www.arcofappalachia.org/simon-woods;https://www.arcofappalachia.org/simon-farm		2026-03-31T12:11:18Z	2026-03-31T12:11:18Z
Tremper Mound	Historic Site			Active	Arc of Appalachia	Arc of Appalachia			2,000-year-old Hopewell Culture ceremonial earthwork along the Scioto River. Protects 6.17 miles of forest corridor including 3.56 miles of Pond Creek's main stem and primary headwaters, and 1.30 miles of Scioto River riparian corridor. Famous for discovery of approximately 60 Hopewell effigy pipes carved in the images of local wildlife. Located four miles north of the Portsmouth Works Hopewell ceremonial complex. Over two-thirds of the mound was part of the 618-acre Matthews Farm; entire mound unified under Arc ownership.	20580 SR-73, McDermott, Ohio 45663; main entrance on OH-104 (southbound only); Scioto River eastern boundary	706	Scioto		Rush	38.802385	-83.008597	86CRRX2R+XH	Three hiking trails;main entrance parking lot on OH-104;second trailhead parking (Huckleberry Ridge Trailhead, 0.5 mi south on OH-104);open year-round sunrise to sunset	Baseline seed — previously listed as Tier 8 (private) but Arc of Appalachia is a nonprofit land trust; correctly staged at Tier 7. Tremper Mound is an NRHP-listed Hopewell Culture earthwork — NRHP feature within Tier 7 parcel; public visitor access exists (Tremper Mound Trail .20-mi loop leads directly to mound) — see child entity creation below. Entrance is one-way approach southbound on OH-104 due to dangerous traffic conditions. Baseline seed confirmed.		https://www.arcofappalachia.org/tremper-mound;https://www.arcofappalachia.org/visit-tremper-mound;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/640b875d14fa1852d6031793/t/6812107083f9a510c91e3011/1746014323550/Tremper+Mound+Hiking+Guide.pdf;https://sciotohistorical.org/items/show/148;https://www.sciotoheritagetrail.com/tremper-mound.html		2026-03-31T12:11:18Z	2026-03-31T12:11:18Z
Gladys Riley Golden Star Lily Preserve	Nature Preserve			Active	Arc of Appalachia	Arc of Appalachia	Clean Ohio (expansion acquisition)		First preserve specifically acquired to protect golden star lily (Erythronium rostratum), an endangered Ohio wildflower with an extremely limited geographical range. Floodplain forest along Rocky Fork of Scioto Brush Creek with spring ephemeral wildflowers. Oak-hickory hillside forest with trees of impressive girth. Rocky slopes carpeted with large fern colonies.	Tick Ridge-Koenig Hill Rd, Otway, Ohio 45657	230	Scioto		Brush Creek	38.850620	-83.201882	86CRVQ2X+66	Two hiking trails;gravel trailhead parking lot;open to public	Baseline seed — previously listed as Tier 8 (private) but Arc of Appalachia is a nonprofit land trust; correctly staged at Tier 7. Preserve currently 230 acres (expanded from original 186 ac via 2015 acquisition of 118 acres from Ralstin/Hazelbaker/Ivers family); third expansion of ~40 acres (Rocky Fork confluence with Scioto Brush Creek) pending. DISTINCT from SC-S-0006 (Gladys Riley Golden-star State Nature Preserve, Tier 2, ODNR) — the SNP is an ODNR-designated state nature preserve embedded within the larger Arc preserve. The 186 ac vs. 230 ac discrepancy in prior records reflects the SNP acreage vs. the full Arc preserve acreage. Access: from SR-32 east of Peebles, south on SR-73 12.2 mi through Rarden to Otway; right on SR-348 1.1 mi; left on Rocky Fork Rd 0.2 mi; left on Tick Ridge-Koenig Rd 0.2 mi; parking lot on left after Rocky Fork Bridge. Baseline seed confirmed.		https://www.arcofappalachia.org/gladys-riley;https://www.arcofappalachia.org/visit-gladys-riley;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/640b875d14fa1852d6031793/t/6559056b8df2f945819c3198/1700332908641/Gladys+Riley+Hiking+Guide.pdf;https://birdinghotspots.org/hotspot/L7323121;https://www.sciotoheritagetrail.com/gladys-riley-gold-star-preserve.html		2026-03-31T12:11:18Z	2026-03-31T12:11:18Z
