Otway Covered Bridge	Park			Active	Otway Historical Society	Otway Historical Society	Federal Highway Administration (2012 repair grant)		Only remaining covered bridge in Scioto County. 127-foot Smith type timber truss bridge over Scioto Brush Creek, built 1874 by Smith Bridge Co. of Toledo. Bypassed and closed to vehicle traffic in 1961; acquired by Otway Historical Society and now serves as a historic landmark and public park. Tornado damaged the roof in March 2012; federal grant-funded repair concluded August 2014.	5923 State Route 348, Otway, Ohio 45657; Brush Creek Township; crosses Scioto Brush Creek		Scioto		Brush Creek	38.859320	-83.190600	86CRVR55+PQ	Historic covered bridge (public access);park setting;annual Covered Bridge Festival and Car Show	Baseline seed confirmed. NRHP listed 1974. GPS 38.85932°N, 83.19060°W converted from DMS 38°51.759'N, 83°11.436'W (from HMDB historical marker coordinates). Also referenced at alternate address 341 Curtis Smith Rd, Otway OH 45657. Part of Scioto Heritage Trail. Qualifies as Tier 8 Site (publicly accessible historic structure, Otway Historical Society ownership, identity-bearing). Annual Covered Bridge Festival. Part of the 36-mile Scioto County Shawnee Bridge to Bridge Route (Otway Covered Bridge to Mackletree Bridge).		https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Otway_Covered_Bridge;https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=132962;https://www.sciotoheritagetrail.com/otway-covered-bridge.html;https://historicbridges.org/bridges/browser/?bridgebrowser=ohio/otway/;https://nationalregisterofhistoricplaces.com/OH/Scioto/state.html		2026-03-31T12:11:18Z	2026-03-31T12:11:18Z
